  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nIn a commercial-driver follow-up arranged after an occupational screening concern, the nurse interviews the driver and checks the accompanying documents against the reported sequence of events; the employer wants a quick answer before allocating a vehicle, but the record separates present evidence, historical findings and questions that the clinician has not yet resolved.\n\nThe specialist's completed investigation found no diagnosable cause for a single confirmed blackout, and the signed chronology documents one event with no further events over 4.5 years; the nurse records that this is a blackout of undetermined nature after investigation, rather than an investigation still pending, while an earlier faint in the driver's father is kept separate from the patient's event count and cannot create a recurrent patient history.\n\nThe employer's copied form relates to an earlier period of work and contains a broad satisfactory box without the measurements underlying it, whereas the current nurse entry identifies the source of each specific finding; the driver's wish to continue scheduled duties is recorded as a preference, not as proof that the present assessment has resolved the documented concern.\n\nThe record is prepared for the reviewing clinician with the sequence of events and the provenance of the available findings intact, because the employer summary and the driver's account answer different questions; a completed test is retained as such, but an unresolved detail is not filled in from a family member's history or from an earlier document with different testing conditions.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
